      <h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.125rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text-primary);margin:28px 0 10px;padding-bottom:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-warm);">What Are Cookies</h2><p style="color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.85;margin:0 0 8px;">Cookies are small text files stored on your device when you visit a website. They help us remember your preferences, keep you logged in, understand how you use our platform, and show you relevant content.</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.125rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text-primary);margin:28px 0 10px;padding-bottom:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-warm);">Types of Cookies We Use</h2><p style="color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.85;margin:0 0 8px;"><strong>Essential Cookies:</strong> Required for the platform to function (login sessions, cart contents). Cannot be disabled. <strong>Analytics Cookies:</strong> Google Analytics data to understand usage patterns. Opt-out available. <strong>Marketing Cookies:</strong> Used for personalised advertising on external platforms. Opt-out available in preferences. <strong>Preference Cookies:</strong> Remember your settings (language, location, notification preferences).</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.125rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text-primary);margin:28px 0 10px;padding-bottom:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-warm);">Managing Cookie Preferences</h2><p style="color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.85;margin:0 0 8px;">You can manage cookie preferences at any time by clicking "Cookie Settings" in the website footer, or by adjusting your browser settings. Note that disabling essential cookies may affect platform functionality.</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.125rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text-primary);margin:28px 0 10px;padding-bottom:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-warm);">Third-Party Cookies</h2><p style="color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.85;margin:0 0 8px;">We use Google Analytics (analytics), Meta Pixel (advertising), Razorpay (payment security), and Delhivery/Shiprocket (delivery tracking). Each third party has its own privacy policy governing how they use data from their cookies.</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.125rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text-primary);margin:28px 0 10px;padding-bottom:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-warm);">Cookie Retention</h2><p style="color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.85;margin:0 0 8px;">Session cookies expire when you close your browser. Persistent cookies have varying lifetimes — typically 30 days to 1 year. Analytics cookies are retained for 26 months by default (Google Analytics standard).</p><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.125rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text-primary);margin:28px 0 10px;padding-bottom:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border-warm);">Contact</h2><p style="color:var(--text-secondary);line-height:1.85;margin:0 0 8px;">For questions about our cookie policy, contact privacy@consciousindi.com.</p>
